liblo
    https://liblo.sourceforge.net
    GNU Lesser General Public License, Version 2.1 or later.
    Used only for NSM session management (src/nsm.cpp), which is a Linux
    session-management protocol; the macOS and Windows builds neither link nor
    contain liblo at all (src/nsmStub.cpp stands in for src/nsm.cpp there).
    On Linux it is linked dynamically. No liblo code is incorporated into
    Luvie's binaries: under section 5 of the LGPL such a binary is "a work that
    uses the Library" and falls outside that licence's terms. Should liblo ever
    be vendored or statically linked, section 6 would apply and a copy of the
    LGPL would have to ship with it.

    One distribution format is an exception. The Linux AppImage is a
    self-contained bundle, so it carries a copy of liblo.so alongside the other
    shared libraries it needs, and section 6 does apply to it. Its obligations
    are met inside the AppImage itself: LICENSES/bundled/ holds each bundled
    library's licence and names where liblo's complete corresponding source can
    be obtained, and liblo remains a separate, replaceable dynamic library that
    the user can substitute (extract with --appimage-extract, replace
    usr/lib/liblo.so.7, repack). See tools/make-appimage.sh, which assembles
    that directory from the libraries actually bundled rather than from a
    hand-written list, so a new dependency cannot ship undocumented. The
    tarball and .deb bundle nothing and are unaffected.


